---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import Terminal from '../../components/Terminal.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Models"
  seoTitle="AI Model and Provider Support in ostk"
  description="Compare ostk model and provider integrations, driver features, local routes, configuration precedence, and verified portability boundaries."
  sectionLabel="GET_STARTED // MODEL_SELECTION"
>
  <p class="font-headline text-lg text-on-surface-variant italic leading-relaxed max-w-xl mb-4">
    ostk has a provider-neutral scheduling interface with direct, gateway, and local routes. A route existing in code is not the same as every model version being verified: tool schemas, streaming, reasoning, and usage accounting vary by integration.
  </p>
  <p class="font-body text-xs text-secondary leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-12">
    Canonical project tasks, decisions, pages, and audit remain local across routes. Full conversation continuity is a separate capability. Generic MCP clients load stored pages inline; Anthropic sessions can additionally use Anthropic Files for context efficiency and cross-host recovery. Check the route status and last-verified evidence before treating a model switch as a product guarantee.
  </p>

  <!-- Provider table -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="section-label mb-6">PROVIDERS</h2>
    <div class="space-y-px">
      {[
        {
          name: 'Anthropic',
          models: 'claude-* models supported by the configured Anthropic API version',
          context: '200k tokens',
          wire: 'Native',
          level: 'FULL',
          features: 'Tool use, extended thinking, streaming, prompt caching, vision, file upload, batch API, token counting, model listing, speed mode, citations',
          key: 'ANTHROPIC_API_KEY',
          src: 'src/cpu/anthropic.rs:257–297',
        },
        {
          name: 'Google Gemini',
          models: 'gemini-* models supported by the configured Google API version',
          context: '1M tokens',
          wire: 'Gemini API adapter',
          level: 'FULL',
          features: 'Tool use, thinking (auto for 3.x models, thinkingLevel: HIGH), streaming. No client-side prompt caching — server-side only.',
          key: 'GEMINI_API_KEY (or GOOGLE_API_KEY)',
          src: 'src/cpu/gemini.rs:32–70, 299–319',
        },
        {
          name: 'Mistral',
          models: 'mistral-*, codestral*, ministral*, devstral*, magistral*',
          context: '256k tokens',
          wire: 'OpenAI-compat',
          level: 'FULL',
          features: 'Tool use, streaming. No thinking mode. ostk handles Mistral-specific quirks: tool name injection (required by API), tool ID remapping (9 alphanumeric chars).',
          key: 'MISTRAL_API_KEY',
          src: 'src/cpu/mistral.rs:24–45, 145–220',
        },
        {
          name: 'OpenAI',
          models: 'gpt-*, o1*, o3*, o4*',
          context: 'Model/version-dependent',
          wire: 'Native Responses API',
          level: 'IMPLEMENTED',
          features: 'Tool use, streaming, encrypted reasoning continuity where supported. Verify the exact model/version in the compatibility evidence.',
          key: 'OPENAI_API_KEY',
          src: 'src/cpu/openai.rs, src/cpu/providers.rs:111–120',
        },
        {
          name: 'OpenRouter',
          models: 'Explicit openrouter/<provider>/<model> and supported org/model routes',
          context: 'Model-dependent',
          wire: 'OpenAI-compatible gateway',
          level: 'GATEWAY',
          features: 'Tool use and streaming when the selected upstream preserves the expected OpenAI-compatible semantics. Not a universal fallback or feature-parity promise.',
          key: 'OPENROUTER_API_KEY',
          src: 'src/cpu/openrouter.rs:12–51',
        },
        {
          name: 'Ollama (local)',
          models: 'local/<model>, ollama/<model>, or model:tag',
          context: 'Model-dependent',
          wire: 'OpenAI-compatible local endpoint',
          level: 'LOCAL / MODEL-SPECIFIC',
          features: 'Tool use and streaming depend on the loaded model and Ollama build. Models with a ":" separator auto-route here.',
          key: 'None required (OLLAMA_HOST to override endpoint)',
          src: 'src/cpu/mod.rs:437–454, providers.rs:62–68',
        },
        {
          name: 'Apple on-device',
          models: 'apple/default',
          context: '4k tokens',
          wire: 'OpenAI-compat',
          level: 'EXPERIMENTAL',
          features: 'Streaming only. macOS only. Routes to the olleh local service on port 11941. Suitable for preprocessing, not primary agent work.',
          key: 'None (APPLE_MODEL_HOST to override)',
          src: 'src/cpu/mod.rs:439–446, model_registry.rs:196–201',
        },
      ].map(p => (
        <div class="bg-surface-container-low">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-0">
            <div class="md:col-span-2 bg-surface-container px-4 py-5 flex md:flex-col justify-between md:justify-start items-baseline md:items-start gap-2 md:gap-0">
              <span class="font-body text-sm font-bold text-primary">{p.name}</span>
              <span class="font-label text-[9px] text-outline uppercase tracking-widest md:mt-1">{p.level}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="md:col-span-10 p-5">
              <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs font-body">
                <div class="min-w-0">
                  <div class="font-label text-[10px] text-primary mb-1">MODELS</div>
                  <code class="text-secondary text-[11px] break-words">{p.models}</code>
                </div>
                <div class="min-w-0">
                  <div class="font-label text-[10px] text-primary mb-1">CONTEXT / WIRE</div>
                  <span class="text-secondary break-words">{p.context} — {p.wire}</span>
                </div>
                <div class="md:col-span-2 min-w-0">
                  <div class="font-label text-[10px] text-primary mb-1">FEATURES</div>
                  <span class="text-secondary break-words">{p.features}</span>
                </div>
                <div class="min-w-0">
                  <div class="font-label text-[10px] text-outline mb-1">API KEY</div>
                  <code class="text-secondary text-[11px] break-words">{p.key}</code>
                </div>
                <div class="min-w-0">
                  <div class="font-label text-[10px] text-outline mb-1">SOURCE</div>
                  <code class="text-secondary text-[10px] break-words">{p.src}</code>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="bg-surface-container-low p-5 border-l-2 border-primary mt-6 max-w-2xl">
      <div class="font-label text-[10px] text-primary mb-2">ADDITIONAL_IMPLEMENTED_ROUTES</div>
      <p class="font-body text-xs text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        The current kernel also contains direct bare-prefix routes for DeepSeek, Moonshot/Kimi, and xAI, plus an Apple-Silicon MLX route with a managed <code class="text-primary">mlx_lm.server</code> lifecycle. These are implemented code paths, not a claim that every current model version has passed an end-to-end acceptance run. Consult dated compatibility evidence before publishing a supported badge.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FROM auto -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="serif-text text-3xl font-medium text-on-surface mb-4">How <code>FROM auto</code> Picks a Model</h2>
    <p class="font-body text-xs text-secondary mb-6 max-w-lg">
      When an Agentfile says <code class="text-primary">FROM auto</code> (or no <code>FROM</code> at all), ostk scores available models based on which API keys are present. Source: <code class="text-primary">src/commands/run.rs:89–197</code>.
    </p>
    <div class="space-y-px">
      {[
        { step: '01', check: 'Runtime override: staging/preferred_model (set by :model in TUI)' },
        { step: '02', check: 'HUMANFILE MODEL directive (highest-priority static config)' },
        { step: '03', check: 'HUMANFILE FALLBACK directive (secondary static config)' },
        { step: '04', check: 'Environment scoring: scan for API keys and rank by capability. claude-opus-4-6 + ANTHROPIC_API_KEY scores 100; claude-sonnet-4-6 scores 90; gpt-4o + OPENAI_API_KEY scores 60; gemini-2.0-flash + GEMINI_API_KEY scores 50.' },
        { step: '05', check: 'Default fallback: claude-sonnet-4-6 (run.rs:196)' },
      ].map(s => (
        <div class="bg-surface-container grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12">
          <div class="md:col-span-1 bg-surface-container-low flex items-center justify-center py-3">
            <span class="serif-text text-lg font-bold text-primary">{s.step}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="md:col-span-11 px-4 py-3">
            <span class="font-body text-xs text-secondary">{s.check}</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="font-body text-xs text-secondary mt-4 max-w-lg">
      <code class="text-primary">OSTK_MODEL</code> env var overrides everything — if set, it's used regardless of HUMANFILE or FROM. Source: <code class="text-primary">src/cpu/context.rs:116</code>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Config surface -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="section-label mb-4">CONFIGURATION</h2>
    <p class="font-body text-xs text-secondary mb-6 max-w-lg">
      Four places to set a model, in priority order:
    </p>
    <div class="bg-surface-container-low p-6 border-l-2 border-primary">
      {[
        { method: 'OSTK_MODEL env var', scope: 'Session-wide override. Ignores everything else.', example: 'OSTK_MODEL=gemini-2.5-pro ostk run agents/worker.af' },
        { method: 'FROM <model> in Agentfile', scope: 'Per-agent. The agent always runs this model.', example: 'FROM claude-sonnet-4-6' },
        { method: 'HUMANFILE MODEL directive', scope: 'Project-wide default. Applies when FROM is auto or absent.', example: 'MODEL claude-opus-4-6' },
        { method: '--model flag on ostk kernel spawn', scope: 'Per-spawn override. Takes precedence over Agentfile FROM auto.', example: 'ostk kernel spawn worker --model gemini-2.5-pro "task"' },
      ].map(c => (
        <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-2 md:gap-4 text-xs font-body py-3 border-b border-surface-variant">
          <span class="text-primary md:w-52 md:shrink-0 font-bold break-words">{c.method}</span>
          <span class="text-secondary flex-1 break-words">{c.scope}</span>
          <code class="text-outline md:shrink-0 text-[10px] break-words">{c.example}</code>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Feature matrix -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="section-label mb-4">FEATURE_MATRIX</h2>
    <p class="font-body text-xs text-secondary mb-6 max-w-lg">
      Not every provider supports every feature. The CpuDriver trait provides a common surface, but the underlying APIs vary. This matrix shows what actually works per provider at the driver level.
    </p>
    <div class="bg-surface-container-low p-6 border-l-2 border-primary overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full font-body text-xs">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-surface-variant">
            <th class="pb-3 pr-3 text-left font-label text-[10px] text-primary uppercase tracking-widest">Feature</th>
            <th class="pb-3 pr-2 text-center font-label text-[9px] text-outline uppercase">Anthropic</th>
            <th class="pb-3 pr-2 text-center font-label text-[9px] text-outline uppercase">Gemini</th>
            <th class="pb-3 pr-2 text-center font-label text-[9px] text-outline uppercase">Mistral</th>
            <th class="pb-3 pr-2 text-center font-label text-[9px] text-outline uppercase">OpenAI</th>
            <th class="pb-3 pr-2 text-center font-label text-[9px] text-outline uppercase">Ollama</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {[
            { f: 'Tool use', a: '✓', g: '✓', m: '✓', o: '✓', l: '✓' },
            { f: 'Streaming', a: '✓', g: '✓', m: '✓', o: '✓', l: '✓' },
            { f: 'Extended thinking', a: '✓', g: '✓ (3.x)', m: '—', o: 'built-in*', l: '—' },
            { f: 'Prompt caching', a: '✓', g: 'server', m: '—', o: '—', l: '—' },
            { f: 'Vision/images', a: '✓', g: '✓', m: '✓', o: '✓', l: 'model' },
            { f: 'File upload API', a: '✓', g: '—', m: '—', o: '—', l: '—' },
            { f: 'Token counting', a: '✓', g: '—', m: '—', o: '—', l: '—' },
            { f: 'Batch API', a: '✓', g: '—', m: '—', o: '—', l: '—' },
            { f: 'Speed mode', a: '✓', g: '—', m: '—', o: '—', l: '—' },
            { f: 'Citations', a: '✓', g: '—', m: '—', o: '—', l: '—' },
          ].map(r => (
            <tr class="border-b border-surface-variant/50">
              <td class="py-2 pr-3 font-bold text-on-surface">{r.f}</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-2 text-center text-secondary">{r.a}</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-2 text-center text-secondary">{r.g}</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-2 text-center text-secondary">{r.m}</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-2 text-center text-secondary">{r.o}</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-2 text-center text-secondary">{r.l}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="font-body text-xs text-secondary mt-4 max-w-lg">
      <span class="text-primary">✓</span> = the selected driver implements a translation path, not that every current model version is acceptance-tested. <span class="text-primary">—</span> = not available in that driver. <span class="text-primary">server</span> = provider-managed. <span class="text-primary">built-in*</span> = reasoning is model behavior. <span class="text-primary">model</span> = depends on the loaded Ollama model. Direct DeepSeek, Moonshot, xAI, OpenRouter, and MLX routes require their own compatibility evidence and are not implied by this selected-driver table.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Model-specific notes -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="section-label mb-4">MODEL_SPECIFIC_NOTES</h2>
    <div class="bg-surface-container-low p-6 border-l-2 border-primary">
      <div class="space-y-4 font-body text-xs text-secondary">
        <div>
          <span class="text-primary font-bold">Gemini 3.x thinking:</span> When the model name contains "3.1" or "3-", the driver automatically sends <code class="text-primary">thinkingConfig.includeThoughts: true</code> and <code class="text-primary">thinkingLevel: "HIGH"</code>. Gemini 2.x models get standard config only. Source: <code class="text-primary">gemini.rs:105–121</code>.
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="text-primary font-bold">Mistral tool ID remapping:</span> Mistral requires tool call IDs to be exactly 9 alphanumeric characters. Anthropic emits <code class="text-primary">toolu_</code> prefixed IDs that are longer. ostk remaps them transparently. Source: <code class="text-primary">mistral.rs:191–220</code>.
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="text-primary font-bold">Ollama auto-detection:</span> Any model name containing a colon (e.g., <code class="text-primary">codestral:22b</code>) is auto-routed to Ollama without the <code class="text-primary">local/</code> prefix. Source: <code class="text-primary">model_registry.rs:251–253</code>.
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="text-primary font-bold">OpenAI routing:</span> Bare <code class="text-primary">gpt-*</code> and o-series names use the native OpenAI Responses driver and fail if its required key is unavailable. Use an explicit <code class="text-primary">openrouter/...</code> model identifier when you intend to route through OpenRouter. Source: <code class="text-primary">providers.rs:111–120</code>.
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="text-primary font-bold">DeepSeek routing:</span> Bare <code class="text-primary">deepseek-*</code> identifiers use the direct DeepSeek endpoint and fail closed without <code class="text-primary">DEEPSEEK_API_KEY</code>. Slash-form <code class="text-primary">deepseek/...</code> identifiers remain explicit OpenRouter routes. Moonshot/Kimi and xAI have analogous direct bare-prefix routes.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Quick example -->
  <section class="mb-16">
    <h2 class="section-label mb-4">QUICK_EXAMPLE</h2>
    <Terminal label="HUMANFILE">
      <pre><span class="text-primary">MODEL</span> claude-sonnet-4-6
<span class="text-primary">FALLBACK</span> gemini-2.5-pro</pre>
    </Terminal>
    <Terminal label="agents/cheap-lint.af">
      <pre><span class="text-primary">FROM</span> local/codestral:22b
<span class="text-primary">PROMPT</span> Run eslint, fix warnings.
<span class="text-primary">TOOL</span> shell
<span class="text-primary">LIMIT</span> budget_usd 0</pre>
    </Terminal>
    <p class="font-body text-xs text-secondary mt-4 max-w-lg">
      The HUMANFILE declares a project default and fallback; the lint agent pins a local route with <code class="text-primary">FROM</code>. Local inference has no provider token charge, although hardware and operational costs remain. Multiple routes can coexist, but preserving canonical project state is not the same as guaranteeing full conversation or feature continuity between them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="metadata-ribbon border-t border-surface-variant">
    <span class="font-label text-[10px] text-secondary mr-4">RELATED:</span>
    <a href="/start/"><Icon name="rocket_launch" size="14" class="align-middle mr-1" />QUICK_START</a>
    <a href="/docs/agentfile/"><Icon name="smart_toy" size="14" class="align-middle mr-1" />AGENTFILE</a>
    <a href="/docs/configuration/#humanfile"><Icon name="person" size="14" class="align-middle mr-1" />HUMANFILE</a>
    <a href="/docs/configuration/#envvars"><Icon name="tune" size="14" class="align-middle mr-1" />ENV_VARS</a>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
